doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22805050

abstract: >-
  Portable Intelligence Runtime Pieces and Units (PIRP/PIRU) develops a
  structural framework for intelligence that can be bounded, carried,
  published, received, localized, continued, composed, validated, relayed,
  and grown across humans, AIs, tools, runtimes, organizations, domains,
  and generations. PIRP represents discovery-oriented Portable Intelligence
  whose useful runtime structure may precede complete computational
  classification, while PIRU represents a more formalized, bounded, typed,
  and reusable engineering unit. The framework extends Portable Intelligence
  into Open PIRPs for unresolved intelligence, publishing as intelligence
  transfer, Relay Context, Knowledge and Relay CallingGraphs, Relay
  Localization, the PIRP Dispatch Plane, Collective Learning, and
  Computational Growth. It further proposes that the history of how
  intelligence is received, transformed, continued, and grown can itself
  become reusable structural intelligence.

